      "body": "### Finding Description and Impact\n\nPersonal utilization for rewards is derived from epoch-to-epoch utilization deltas without time weighting or minimum holding duration. As a result, utilization added immediately before epoch end is treated as if it represented meaningful epoch participation.\n\nThis how the vulneralbility arises :\n\n1. Attacker performs a boundary deposit right before epoch end `e`.\n   - `deposit()` adds utilization using full `msg.value` before reward calculations:\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/MultiVault.sol:676-679\n_addUtilization(receiver, int256(msg.value));\nreturn _processDeposit(msg.sender, receiver, termId, curveId, msg.value, minShares);\n```\n\n2. Utilization is written directly into current epoch buckets.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/MultiVault.sol:1488-1492\ntotalUtilization[epoch] += totalValue;\npersonalUtilization[user][epoch] += totalValue;\n```\n\n3. At epoch transition, rollover preserves prior epoch exposure snapshots and supports boundary sensitivity.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/MultiVault.sol:1531-1534, 1544-1547\ntotalUtilization[currentEpochLocal] = totalUtilization[previousEpoch];\n...\npersonalUtilization[user][currentEpochLocal] = lastEpochUtilization;\n```\n\n4. In epoch `e+1`, claim logic always targets `prevEpoch = e`.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol:361-371\nuint256 prevEpoch = currentEpochLocal - 1;\nuint256 rawUserRewards = _userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(msg.sender, prevEpoch);\nuint256 personalUtilizationRatio = _getPersonalUtilizationRatio(msg.sender, prevEpoch);\nuint256 userRewards = rawUserRewards * personalUtilizationRatio / BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR;\n```\n\n5. Personal utilization ratio is driven by epoch delta, not hold time.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol:509-514, 537-539\nint256 userUtilizationBefore = IMultiVault(multiVault).getUserUtilizationInEpoch(_account, _epoch - 1);\nint256 userUtilizationAfter = IMultiVault(multiVault).getUserUtilizationInEpoch(_account, _epoch);\nint256 rawUtilizationDelta = userUtilizationAfter - userUtilizationBefore;\n...\nif (userUtilizationDelta >= userUtilizationTarget) {\n    return BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR; // 100%\n}\n```\n\n6. `userUtilizationTarget` is last epoch claimed rewards, allowing large one-epoch jumps to max ratio.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol:524\nuint256 userUtilizationTarget = userClaimedRewardsForEpoch[_account][_epoch - 1];\n```\n\n7. Attacker exits shortly after claim; removal impacts current epoch (`e+1`) accounting, not already-claimed epoch `e`.\n```solidity\n// src/protocol/MultiVault.sol:836-839\n(uint256 rawAssetsBeforeFees, uint256 assetsAfterFees) = _processRedeem(...);\n_removeUtilization(receiver, int256(rawAssetsBeforeFees));\n```\n\n8. Net effect:\n   - Epoch `e` claim remains boosted from boundary deposit.\n   - Round-trip cost is mostly fees/slippage paid on unwind in epoch `e+1`.\n   - In one run, reward differential already exceeds realized unwind cost.\n\nAttack path :\n\n1. Attacker keeps baseline stake comparable to passive users.\n2. At `epochTimestampEnd(e) - 1`, attacker makes a temporary deposit to increase personal utilization for epoch `e`.\n3. In epoch `e+1`, attacker calls `claimRewards` and receives boosted rewards for epoch `e`.\n4. Attacker exits the temporary position shortly after boundary.\n5. PoC demonstrates one-run impact using this boundary method.\n\nTimeline example :\n\n1. End of epoch `e`: attacker deposits to inflate `personalUtilization[user][e]`.\n2. Start of epoch `e+1`: attacker calls `claimRewards`, which computes rewards for epoch `e`.\n3. Same epoch `e+1`: attacker redeems temporary position and realizes bounded trading/fee loss.\n4. Result: reward delta from boosted ratio can exceed realized unwind loss\n\nThe impact because of this issue are inflated reward capture by boundary-timing users, dilution of honest users who do not run the timing strategy and extraction pressure on emissions distribution from boundary-timing behavior.\n\n### Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\nPreferred fix:\n  - In `MultiVault`, track cumulative `utilization * time` for each user and for the system, settling the accumulator on every `_addUtilization(...)`, `_removeUtilization(...)`, and epoch rollover.\n  - In `TrustBonding._getPersonalUtilizationRatio(...)`, replace the current end-of-epoch snapshot delta with the delta between consecutive epoch-average utilizations.\n  - This keeps the existing “increase usage relative to last epoch” design, but removes the ability for a one-second boundary deposit to count like a full-epoch contribution.\n\nSimpler safe fallback if a full integral is too invasive:\n  - make utilization added in epoch `e` ineligible for epoch `e` rewards and only count it starting in epoch `e+1`,\n  - or enforce a minimum in-epoch residency before new utilization is included in the ratio path.",
